            <div xml:id="d546">

                <pb facs="0487" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/781.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Governor of
                        California.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt of your telegram of the 13th instant,
                    referred to the Department by the President. The complaint made by Gen. Torres
                    against the alleged violation of neutrality laws will be promptly investigated
                    by the proper Federal authorities and I shall be glad to inform you of the
                    result.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d546-a1.xml" xpointer="d546-a1"/>
